        "original_id": "d2187587-3365-57c3-8ec8-2cf0ac466056",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Topics: Plant genera and botanical classification\n- Concepts: Native range, growth form, species count\n- Products: Bactris, Epigaea\n\nFacts:\n- Bactris is a genus of spiny palms native to Mexico, Central America, South America, and the Caribbean.\n- Most Bactris species are small trees about 2 meters tall, but some Bactris species are large trees and others are shrubs with subterranean stems.\n- Epigaea is a genus of flowering plants in the Ericaceae that comprises three species.",
